  #[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(4.9)")
   $ q G'_k tilde.op p^(*) H_k - q Xi'_k . $ <eq:conormal-local-cartier>]
  After clearing the global indices of $Xi'_k$, the right side is Cartier.
    Hence the locally chosen integral $G'_k$ is $bb(Q)$-Cartier.
    This local assertion follows from the displayed identity;
    ordinary global $bb(Q)$-factoriality supplied the index of the globally defined $Xi'_k$.
    The actual adjoint in (4.8), together with the globally $bb(Q)$-Cartier boundary $B'_S$,
    also makes a reflexive canonical power on $S'$ an actual line.
    The same local generation argument supplies a meromorphic canonical generator if a local Weil representative
    is needed for the vanishing statement.
  Equations (4.8) and (4.9) give
