    unconditionally in dimension at most four. Its analytic positivity and canonical-sheaf conventions are the
    ones in use here. Apply it to $\( X' \, Delta' \)$, then enlarge the generated degree to a multiple of the
    original index. All sections are pullbacks. A section nonzero at a chosen point above $x in
    X$ descends to a section nonzero at $x$; Nakayama’s lemma gives the evaluation surjectivity on $X$. ◻
]

